data: {"id":"202609190929383716e2795f7849c0","created":1789781379,"object":"chat.completion.chunk","model":"glm-5.3-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_5b536f0800764900bf34c6c4","index":0,"type":"function","function":{"name":"submit_context_selection","arguments":"{\"context_read_ids\":[\"53c3ebf49a0123958b99aae4ec51fe22f8165bbc5d21f91d94eec3c63e0bdb2e\", \"70e1ef0633c8fc0fa7402b47951771a408b2d6ae0e4f647da1a79b88e191385a\", \"6e5718f8803e7b2c5b9aebb762b48a79c6b83847006e7931f1820eec156898ab\", \"537d720c92c961ef1ee1a83efbb0c2770624bf4c76cd37303311eaa494a13805\"],\"summary\":\"Issue #1241: on first usage of a (re)initialized compression context, the matchstate window started at position 0, so the first input position could be treated as an invalid match reference. Fixed per the suggested approach: added MEM_STATIC ZSTD_window_init() in lib/compress/zstd_compress_internal.h, which zeroes the window but sets base/dictBase to an empty prefix and starts dictLimit/lowLimit/nextSrc at 1 (so the first input position is always a valid match reference, even during first context usage). Replaced the raw memset(&ms->window, 0, ...) in ZSTD_reset_matchState (lib/compress/zstd_compress.c) with ZSTD_window_init(&ms->window). This mirrors the upstream zstd fix for #1241; downstream ZSTD_window_update/window_clear logic then operates with non-zero starting indices.\"}"}}]}}]}

